From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:06:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Research runner: who to research next is read down the phone
 index

Every fifteen minutes the research runner asked who to research next, and
the query held one of the background pool's two connections for 15-16 s
(logs, 15-16 Oct): a DISTINCT ON that sorted all 592,768 score-history rows
to keep the latest row of 3,363 phones.

The latest row per phone is now found by walking the existing
(phone, built_at DESC) index one phone at a time. Same answer on
production (identical hash of the 20 people it returns), 3.4 s against
0.75 s with the round trip.

